<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Olite</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Olite is a town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-navarre">Navarre</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pamplona">Pamplona</a>. In the 15th century it was a favourite residence of the kings of Navarre, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-iii-of-navarre">Charles III the Noble</a> built its large Gothic royal palace with towers, gardens and galleries. The palace, burned during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peninsular-war">Peninsular War</a>, was restored in the 20th century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/olite.jpg" alt="Olite" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: César Viteri Ramirez from Madrid, Spain · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:WLM14ES_-_Castle_of_Olite_-Castillo_de_Olite_-_Multimaniaco.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
